					<meta property="og:description" content="While I am not pleased entirely with the AI art usage, I do understand the circumstances. As a beginner artist myself, I am slightly disappointed in that that, since there are some elements, particularly CGs, which I found really good looking, beautiful even . Were different AI models used for the art production? Because I particularly found strange that the art is very presentable and it does not at least at first glance anyway, have the usual trappings of AI image generation.">
					<meta property="twitter:description" content="While I am not pleased entirely with the AI art usage, I do understand the circumstances. As a beginner artist myself, I am slightly disappointed in that that, since there are some elements, particularly CGs, which I found really good looking, beautiful even . Were different AI models used for the art production? Because I particularly found strange that the art is very presentable and it does not at least at first glance anyway, have the usual trappings of AI image generation.">
			
	
